From 7ab2d16742ba342e480a8931be629e2b24de9ee8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:53:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Add hwc.info service (libhwcservice) for HDCP

Port of the Intel drm-hwcomposer fork hwc.info vndbinder service
(fork commits 56c1a5b, 5167ccd) used by Intel HDCP clients.

The service itself (libhwcservice, libhwcservicelib, hwcservice_test)
is hand-written binder code, which Soong allows only under vendor/ and
hardware/. It is carried in vendor/intel/hardware/interfaces
(graphic/hwcservice); this patch adds only the HWC side:

 - intel/hwcservice/hwcservice_ops.h: C ops table between the HWC and
   libhwcservicelib, exported as libhwcservice_ops_headers.
 - DrmHwc dlopen()s /vendor/lib64/hw/libhwcservicelib.so on a detached
   thread (optional; logged when absent) and maps the HDCP session
   calls to HwcDisplay::StartHdcp()/StopHdcp() of the display driven by
   the connector.
 - The service is started once and lives for the whole process, while
   DrmHwc instances come and go (one per composer client). Calls reach
   the DrmHwc registered as owner under a mutex; ~DrmHwc() unregisters
   under the same mutex, so a transaction never uses a destroyed
   instance. The ops table carries no instance pointer.
 - The requested content type is passed through. HWCS_CP_CONTENT_TYPE1
   requires HDCP 2.2 or newer, so HwcDisplay::StartHdcp() and
   HdcpController::Start() take allow_type0_fallback: for Type 1
   requests a failed Type 1 negotiation ends HDCP instead of retrying
   with Type 0 (HDCP 1.4). Type 0 requests and the composer3 path keep
   the Type 1 -> Type 0 fallback.

The existing sepolicy (hwc_info_service, vndservice_contexts) and the
vendor libbinder (/dev/vndbinder) are used as before.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1589
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
